; ent.example. is an empty non-terminal (only deep.ent.example. exists), and
; *.example. must not apply below it.
;
; No RRSIG(SOA) and no NSEC/NSEC3 chain on purpose: a signed SOA makes the
; non-existence provers run, and they reject a zone without a chain.  The
; RRSIG(DS) only has to be present; it is never verified.
example.           300 IN SOA   ns.example. hostmaster.example. 1 3600 600 86400 300
example.           300 IN NS    ns.example.
ns.example.        300 IN A     10.53.0.1
deep.ent.example.  300 IN A     192.0.2.1
*.example.         300 IN A     198.51.100.45
child.example.     300 IN NS    ns.child.example.
child.example.     300 IN DS    10437 13 2 1C4E708E9DAF795A6CE11798210987899FD04AEDFB71D2093334C5E53DDB4FD8
ns.child.example.  300 IN A     192.0.2.60
foo.example.       300 IN CNAME bar.example.
bar.example.       300 IN A     192.0.2.2

child.example.     300 IN RRSIG DS 13 2 300 20940101000000 20200101000000 10437 example. AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA=
